From 4b10e24d53a43921451687c0d3996311b4dbfc7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 13:21:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/43] cef: expose POSIX window ABI on AROS

Reuse CEF's non-X11 opaque window structures for the initial AROS Ozone/Aura port and select the matching generated platform API hash.

AI_PHASE: chromium-aros-cef

AI_STATUS: focused-object-passed

AI_ASSUMPTION: the Linux non-X11 CEF window structure remains ABI-compatible with AROS while window handles are opaque

AI_VALIDATION: command_line_ctocpp compiled with CEF_API_HASH_PLATFORM and prior browser wrapper objects no longer report missing window handles or CefWindowInfo

AI_LIMITATIONS: the ABI is intentionally shared with Linux until AROS needs platform-specific public fields; GetHead macro collision remains

AI_DECISION_CHAIN:
---
 include/cef_api_hash.h             | 4 ++--
 include/cef_base.h                 | 2 +-
 include/internal/cef_types.h       | 2 +-
 include/internal/cef_types_linux.h | 4 ++--
 tools/make_api_hash_header.py      | 2 +-
 5 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

